WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.873
After many days of summer, the riverbank was busy.

2
00:00:19.874 --> 00:00:23.540
Rat watched the birds packing their nests.

3
00:00:23.541 --> 00:00:27.733
"Why do they have to fly south?" thought Rat.

4
00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:31.417
"The riverbank is perfectly fine."

5
00:00:31.418 --> 00:00:35.762
"Hey, Ratty!" called some mice.

6
00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:37.479
"Come and help."

7
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:41.745
They walked by carrying baskets and boxes.

8
00:00:41.746 --> 00:00:44.403
"What are you up to?" asked Rat.

9
00:00:44.404 --> 00:00:49.140
"Moving! To our winter home," said one mouse.

10
00:00:49.141 --> 00:00:53.142
"But it's a beautiful day," said Rat.

11
00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:55.600
"Winter is far away."

12
00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:59.734
"Oh, we know that," said another mouse.

13
00:00:59.735 --> 00:01:02.201
"But we like to be ready!"

14
00:01:02.202 --> 00:01:05.747
"Let's go for a row," said Rat.

15
00:01:05.748 --> 00:01:07.744
"We can have a picnic!"

16
00:01:07.745 --> 00:01:11.087
"Not today, Rat!" said the first mouse.

17
00:01:11.088 --> 00:01:14.951
"Ask another day, when no one is busy."

18
00:01:14.952 --> 00:01:20.291
Rat frowned. "Fine! Do what you want!"

19
00:01:20.292 --> 00:01:24.281
He turned and tripped over a box.

20
00:01:24.282 --> 00:01:28.335
"Ow!" cried Rat, rubbing his back.

21
00:01:28.336 --> 00:01:32.272
"Be more careful," said a bluebird.

22
00:01:32.273 --> 00:01:34.891
"Be quiet," said Rat.

23
00:01:34.892 --> 00:01:37.004
"I don't need any advice."

24
00:01:37.005 --> 00:01:40.545
Birds flew around Rat's head.

25
00:01:40.546 --> 00:01:43.551
"What's the hurry?" Rat yelled at them.

26
00:01:43.552 --> 00:01:46.722
"We're not going yet," said a robin.

27
00:01:46.723 --> 00:01:48.544
"But we will!"

28
00:01:48.545 --> 00:01:52.353
"Why don't you stay this year?" asked Rat.

29
00:01:52.354 --> 00:01:54.750
"You always like it here."

30
00:01:54.751 --> 00:01:57.680
"We have to go," said the bluebird.

31
00:01:57.681 --> 00:02:00.467
"The south calls us!"

32
00:02:00.468 --> 00:02:05.351
Before long, the mice and the birds were off.

33
00:02:05.352 --> 00:02:08.939
Rat heard footsteps and turned around.

34
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.139
A visitor stood in the road.

35
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:17.920
It was a dusty rat in a sailor's cap.
